Cage: apply the MOUSE SPEED setting to mice and touchpads.

Cage 0.2.0 leaves libinput's pointer acceleration at its default. This reads a
number from /var/lib/couchliteos/mouse-speed (the launcher writes it), clamps
it to libinput's -1..1 and sets it as the acceleration speed of every pointer
device that has one: when the device is added, and again for all pointers on
SIGHUP, which the launcher sends after the setting changes. A missing or
malformed file leaves (or puts back) libinput's default speed, and so does
gamepad-nav's "CouchLiteOS Controller Mouse", which has its own CONTROLLER
MOUSE SPEED setting. Links libinput, which wlroots' libinput backend already
brings into the image.
Applied after cage-0.2.0-osk-panel.patch with patch -p1 by
config/live-build/hooks/live/0050-cage.hook.chroot.
